From 50eac57f6838ad563a9b88d49716f27f8261e4b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <webmaster@palmit.com.au>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:48:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a 5xx that says it queued the request for the model
 rests that model alone, not the account (#3213, liubai0106)

A provider that answers a per-model queue refusal with a 5xx (Qoder's
503 "Qoder queued the request for <model> (this plan's queue: p3); try
again in 30s") fell to failOther and rested the whole account: its other
models, not in that queue, were refused without being asked, and a group
with two accounts failed over between them on the one model that was out,
paying a whole-account rest each time. A 5xx in those words (queuedWords)
rests the model alone now, keyed by restID with its backoff counted
apart, as a refusal over the model alone already does (modelRefused). A
5xx that says nothing of a queue rests the account as before.

Verified with GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.8, umask 022 (this box's Go 1.27.1 and
umask 0027 make four unrelated tests red on main; both pinned):

- TestQueuedModelRestsAlone is red without the change (the reporter's
  refusal rests qoder@u@x.com, the account) and green with it: the model
  rests on its restID, the account's glm-5.3 doesn't, and a plain 503
  still rests the account. TestRest*, TestModelLadder*,
  TestCodeAssistMissingModelRestsTheModel and TestRemoteMagpie* pass.
- gofmt -l clean; go vet, GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui and GOOS=windows
  go vet clean; go build, GOOS=linux go build -tags nogui and GOOS=windows
  go build pass.
- go test -tags nogui ./... -timeout 45m: 67 ok. Red, on main before this
  change too: TestPluginSOCKSProxy (#2207, this box's Bun) and
  TestClaudeClientCacheAbsentUnchanged (#3280).
- Not tried against the real Qoder upstream: the refusal is the one the
  reporter quoted, byte for byte; the wording, not the vendor, decides.
